#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nudge a lane session that has gone quiet. Run it from cron or launchd every 30 minutes.

A lane can stop with nothing set to wake it: its last job ends, the agent replies once and sits at the prompt.
`rh lanes cadence` notices, but only on the lane's delivery window (often a day), and only if someone runs it.
Detection without delivery does nothing, so this script delivers. When a lane's tmux pane is idle (no transcript
write for --idle-min, and no running shell or agent shown in the pane) AND either cadence is WARN/STALLED/BROKEN
or the pane has simply been idle that long, it types one resume prompt into the pane. That happens at most once
per --reask seconds per lane.

Sessions are tmux sessions named PREFIX + owner_session (default prefix `claude-`). Idle time is measured from the
last real turn (a user or assistant message) in the session's Claude Code transcript, never from the file's mtime:
11-08 to 11-11 every lane slept because idle compaction and session metadata rewrote transcripts about hourly, so
no pane ever looked idle and nothing was nudged for three days. Lanes marked EXEMPT or UNCONFIGURED by cadence,
and names in --skip, are never nudged. --dry prints decisions and types nothing. Run one copy per Mac that hosts
lane sessions; each scans its own tmux (pass --tmux when tmux is not on the scheduler's PATH).

After the Claude weekly reset (read from the usage snapshot claude-usage writes) it types one resume prompt into
every idle Claude session, the conductor included and --skip ignored, once per reset. --reset-only does only that,
for a launchd job every 5 minutes. 11-22: the account reached 100% at 20:38 ET, every session stopped, and the
conductor's wake-up was a session cron that could not fire, so nothing resumed until morning.

A Gemini quota stop on an agy driver (seen above its input box, or noted in DRIVER_STATUS.md) hands the lane to its
Claude Code fallback session (started if missing), and after the reset the agy pane goes back on its own Gemini model
(Neon when unknown) and the fallback is told to hand back. agy never runs Claude (11-27 Ricardo: "we obviously have a
Claude subscription. I think we should focus on Neon when using agy").
"""
